  error: |-
    The input did not match the regular expression /repository source/. Input:
    
    '# Your first session with Alex ACT ONE\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Install the pack, approve activation in one app, then try a read-only reasoning\n' +
      'workflow. You need a working GitHub Copilot setup and Node 24 or newer, but\n' +
      '**no optional runtime tools**, API tokens, or paid services for this example.\n' +
      'Copilot CLI is the reference path below; VS Code also exposes the activation\n' +
      'command. Other hosts have [their own setup steps](install.md#where-alex-act-one-works).\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## 1. Install\n' +
      '\n' +
      'If Alex Mall is not registered, add it in your terminal:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```powershell\n' +
      'copilot plugin marketplace add fabioc-aloha/Alex_Skill_Mall\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Then install the reviewed release:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```powershell\n' +
      'copilot plugin install alex-act-one@alex-mall\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'See the [Mall option](install.md#mall-option) for details. Direct repository\n' +
      'source installs can include unreleased changes and are deprecated.\n' +
      'The repository test candidate is `0.9.0-rc.1`, not a tagged or Mall release;\n' +
      'the [temporary candidate procedure](install.md#testing-the-repository-candidate)\n' +
      'is separate from normal onboarding.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Open a Copilot session and confirm it discovers the installed `bootstrap-core`\n' +
      'and `critical-thinking` skills. If either is missing, stop and check the loaded\n' +
      'plugin root and version; do not activate from an unrelated checkout.\n' +
      'See [installation options](install.md#1-install-the-plugin).\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## 2. Activate\n' +
      '\n' +
      'In the app where you want the always-on instructions, run:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```text\n' +
      '/alex-act-one bootstrap-core\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'If that command is unavailable, ask: "Use the installed Alex ACT ONE\n' +
      'bootstrap-core skill to preview activation. Do not apply it yet."\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Review the installed version, target profile, and proposed file actions.\n' +
      'Activation affects every workspace using that profile, not just this project.\n' +
      'Give approval only for the target and actions you want. Installing the plugin\n' +
      'alone does not activate instructions; repeat activation in each app you use.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'The source-only conflict guard is not in published `v0.8.0`. Review existing\n' +
      'files before approving replacements; do not assume the release will block them.\n' +
      'If blocked in the source candidate, stop and review the\n' +
      '[conflict procedure](../skills/bootstrap-core/SKILL.md#instruction-conflicts);\n' +
      'do not add an overwrite flag to get past it.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## 3. Verify\n' +
      '\n' +
      'After the approved apply, ask the agent:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '```text\n' +
      'Use bootstrap-core to preview the same installed version and target again.\n' +
      'Do not apply or repair anything. Report expectedFiles, every file action,\n' +
      'and the receipt action.\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Success means every current instruction is `preserve`, the receipt action is\n' +
      '`preserve`, and the version and target match the approved preview. After apply,\n' +
      'the script also checks destination hashes and reports `receiptCurrent: true`.\n' +
      'Missing files, replacement actions, or a stale receipt need investigation.\n' +
      '\n' +
      'This verifies files, not that the host has loaded them. Start a new session\n' +
      '(fully restart Scout), then ask the host to list the active Alex instructions\n' +
      'and their source paths. If it cannot expose that evidence, record host loading\n' +
      'as **unverified**. A plausible answer to the next exercise does not prove it.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## 4. Try one workflow\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Paste this into that session:\n' +
      '\n' +
      '<!-- first-workflow -->\n' +
      '```text\n' +
      'Use the critical-thinking skill in act-pass mode.\n' +
      'This is a synthetic dashboard case: someone reports that loading takes\n' +
      '8 seconds and proposes a Rust rewrite or Redis caching. No timings have\n' +
      'been measured beyond that report.\n' +
      'Do not edit or write files. Apart from loading the skill guidance,\n' +
      'do not use tools or commands for this exercise.\n' +
      'Give two plausible explanations, evidence that would disconfirm each,\n' +
      'and the next measurement to collect. Mark what remains unknown rather\n' +
      'than choosing a rewrite or cache without evidence.\n' +
      '```\n' +
      '\n' +
      'Look for competing explanations, evidence that could rule each out, and a\n' +
      'specific next measurement. The response should distinguish the reported delay\n' +
      'from measured facts and leave files unchanged. Exact wording is not the test.\n' +
      'This is one practice case, not evidence of general reliability gains.\n' +
      '\n' +
      '## What to try next\n' +
      '\n' +
      '- [Skills and commands](../README.md#the-skills): choose a workflow for your work.\n' +
      '- [Install and host reference](install.md): Scout, other hosts, optional tools,\n' +
      '  and reinstall boundaries.\n' +
      '- [Roadmap](../ROADMAP.md): the published baseline is `v0.8.0`; repository installs\n' +
      '  can include later source-only repairs and the interaction skill, which are not\n' +
      '  yet released through Mall. The offline galleries are demo-only files to open\n' +
      '  in a browser, not proof your MCP runtime is ready.\n'
    
  code: 'ERR_ASSERTION'
  name: 'AssertionError'
  expected:
  actual: |-
    # Your first session with Alex ACT ONE
    
    Install the pack, approve activation in one app, then try a read-only reasoning
    workflow. You need a working GitHub Copilot setup and Node 24 or newer, but
    **no optional runtime tools**, API tokens, or paid services for this example.
    Copilot CLI is the reference path below; VS Code also exposes the activation
    command. Other hosts have [their own setup steps](install.md#where-alex-act-one-works).
    
    ## 1. Install
    
    If Alex Mall is not registered, add it in your terminal:
    
    ```powershell
    copilot plugin marketplace add fabioc-aloha/Alex_Skill_Mall
    ```
    
    Then install the reviewed release:
    
    ```powershell
    copilot plugin install alex-act-one@alex-mall
    ```
    
    See the [Mall option](install.md#mall-option) for details. Direct repository
    source installs can include unreleased changes and are deprecated.
    The repository test candidate is `0.9.0-rc.1`, not a tagged or Mall release;
    the [temporary candidate procedure](install.md#testing-the-repository-candidate)
    is separate from normal onboarding.
    
    Open a Copilot session and confirm it discovers the installed `bootstrap-core`
    and `critical-thinking` skills. If either is missing, stop and check the loaded
    plugin root and version; do not activate from an unrelated checkout.
    See [installation options](install.md#1-install-the-plugin).
    
    ## 2. Activate
    
    In the app where you want the always-on instructions, run:
    
    ```text
    /alex-act-one bootstrap-core
    ```
    
    If that command is unavailable, ask: "Use the installed Alex ACT ONE
    bootstrap-core skill to preview activation. Do not apply it yet."
    
    Review the installed version, target profile, and proposed file actions.
    Activation affects every workspace using that profile, not just this project.
    Give approval only for the target and actions you want. Installing the plugin
    alone does not activate instructions; repeat activation in each app you use.
    
    The source-only conflict guard is not in published `v0.8.0`. Review existing
    files before approving replacements; do not assume the release will block them.
    If blocked in the source candidate, stop and review the
    [conflict procedure](../skills/bootstrap-core/SKILL.md#instruction-conflicts);
    do not add an overwrite flag to get past it.
    
    ## 3. Verify
    
    After the approved apply, ask the agent:
    
    ```text
    Use bootstrap-core to preview the same installed version and target again.
    Do not apply or repair anything. Report expectedFiles, every file action,
    and the receipt action.
    ```
    
    Success means every current instruction is `preserve`, the receipt action is
    `preserve`, and the version and target match the approved preview. After apply,
    the script also checks destination hashes and reports `receiptCurrent: true`.
    Missing files, replacement actions, or a stale receipt need investigation.
    
    This verifies files, not that the host has loaded them. Start a new session
    (fully restart Scout), then ask the host to list the active Alex instructions
    and their source paths. If it cannot expose that evidence, record host loading
    as **unverified**. A plausible answer to the next exercise does not prove it.
    
    ## 4. Try one workflow
    
    Paste this into that session:
    
    <!-- first-workflow -->
    ```text
    Use the critical-thinking skill in act-pass mode.
    This is a synthetic dashboard case: someone reports that loading takes
    8 seconds and proposes a Rust rewrite or Redis caching. No timings have
    been measured beyond that report.
    Do not edit or write files. Apart from loading the skill guidance,
    do not use tools or commands for this exercise.
    Give two plausible explanations, evidence that would disconfirm each,
    and the next measurement to collect. Mark what remains unknown rather
    than choosing a rewrite or cache without evidence.
    ```
    
    Look for competing explanations, evidence that could rule each out, and a
    specific next measurement. The response should distinguish the reported delay
    from measured facts and leave files unchanged. Exact wording is not the test.
    This is one practice case, not evidence of general reliability gains.
    
    ## What to try next
    
    - [Skills and commands](../README.md#the-skills): choose a workflow for your work.
    - [Install and host reference](install.md): Scout, other hosts, optional tools,
      and reinstall boundaries.
    - [Roadmap](../ROADMAP.md): the published baseline is `v0.8.0`; repository installs
      can include later source-only repairs and the interaction skill, which are not
      yet released through Mall. The offline galleries are demo-only files to open
      in a browser, not proof your MCP runtime is ready.
    
